# Re:Solve Repository Instructions

These rules apply to the entire application repository. Product behavior is governed by the Re:Solve Product Bible; this file carries the durable implementation rules needed inside source control.

## Build scope
- Implement only the current Product Bible/Lovable build slice.
- Do not pre-build adjacent modules or placeholder schemas.
- If a requirement conflicts with established Re:Solve terminology/architecture, report the contradiction instead of silently creating new product truth.

## Product architecture
- One application, two role-shaped shells: Admin OS and Client Portal.
- Workspace, Operating Entity, Organisation, Contact/User/Membership and Property remain distinct concepts.
- Principal-based authorization uses capability + scope and must be enforced server-side.
- Keep provider/data access behind shared services/repositories/connectors where practical.
- Plugins add product capability; Connectors integrate external systems.
- Business truth must not be shaped around one external provider.

## Explicit exclusions
Do not add HR, payroll, recruitment, leave/attendance, employee performance, Timesheets/Time Tracking, or Client Service Consumption/remaining-hours/credit metering.

## External boundaries
- Chatwoot owns support conversations/messages, web chat, routing, support Knowledge and Captain.
- WhatsApp/Baileys is Re:Solve↔client operational communication.
- Àríyá is Re:Solve's built-in AI and remains separate from Chatwoot Captain.
- Billing is payment-provider-neutral; verified provider events establish payment truth.
- Re:Solve owns native Monitoring; Uptime Kuma/external monitors are optional connectors.

## Core UI — mandatory
Use the Re:Solve Core UI Component Framework. shadcn/ui, Untitled UI React and Tremor are mandatory major sources/influences; React Aria/Base UI/Radix and TanStack are approved foundational tools. Normalize reusable patterns into Re:Solve-owned components/tokens rather than library soup.

Application chrome is first-class: Sidebar, TopBar, ResolveAvatar/AccountMenu, Notifications, Search/Command, Quick Create, Àríyá, mobile navigation and global states must remain polished and coherent.

Navigation must remain simple/shallow with clear text labels, closer to Perfex/Brevo clarity. Do not introduce Odoo-style app grids/module launchers, Twenty-style object/module switching as the primary model, icon-only root nav or uncontrolled nested/plugin navigation.

Reusable Core UI changes should be represented in the development Component Gallery.

## UX quality
- Target WCAG 2.2 AA.
- Design phone, tablet, laptop and desktop intentionally.
- PWA/offline behavior is explicit and privacy-safe.
- Include applicable loading, skeleton, empty, first-use, error, partial/stale, permission/read-only, degraded-provider and offline states.
- Sensitive Vault data must never be cached/logged/indexed casually.

## Platform primitives
Keep Attention, Notification, Activity and append-only Audit separate.
Use the Action Registry for reusable consequential mutations so UI, Àríyá, API, MCP and Automations share authorization/risk behavior.
Preserve source/authority/freshness for connector/imported/derived/AI data when material.

## Security
- Hidden UI is not authorization.
- Test negative cross-Organisation/Property access.
- Do not expose secrets in client code, logs, generic search, notifications or AI/MCP context.
- Sensitive/high-risk Actions may require confirmation, approval or step-up.

## Portability
Lovable/Supabase are development tools, not required production runtime assumptions. Avoid Lovable-only product-critical behavior and scattered provider coupling. Keep schema migrations/versioned data and ordinary source-controlled PWA/API/MCP behavior portable.

## Completion
A slice is complete only after acceptance criteria, tests, security/permission, responsive/PWA, accessibility, Core UI/design and relevant portability review. Record intentionally deferred scope.